# Code {{.Slice.ID}}

{{template "header" .}}

## Start

Run `metis kickoff --role coder` and follow it from step 1.

## Brief

{{if .BriefCommitted -}}
The brief at `{{.BriefPath}}` is committed and governs this slice. Read it first; do not widen it.
{{- else if .BriefExists -}}
A brief draft exists at `{{.BriefPath}}` but is not committed. Finish it from the plan section, then `metis commit --brief`, before any code.
{{- else -}}
There is no brief yet. Write it before any code: `metis brief {{.Slice.ID}} --write`, fill it from the plan section (goal, owned_paths, definition of done, test plan), then `metis commit --brief`.
{{- end}}

## Scope

Edit only the files the brief's owned_paths declare. A fix genuinely needed outside them goes in the brief's "Out-of-scope touches" with what, where and why.

## Verify and flip

1. Commit your work with `metis commit -m "<message>"` (stage the files first).
2. `metis verify --post --slice {{.Slice.ID}}` must be green.
3. `metis commit --flip coded --slice {{.Slice.ID}}`.

